PG.notes("s11-intro", "<p class=\"summary\">Introduces Bootstrap as a pre-made CSS framework (2010, from two Twitter developers), weighs its pros and cons, and shows how to add it through a CDN link. A short exercise has the learner add the stylesheet, drop in a Bootstrap card, point its image at a local file and centre it with an override style using Flexbox.</p>\n<h3>What Bootstrap is</h3>\n<ul><li>A CSS framework: a ready-made stylesheet (and optional script) you include in a project and then use by adding class names to your HTML.</li><li>Created in 2010 by two Twitter developers, Mark Otto and Jacob Thornton. It is open source, so its CSS can be browsed on GitHub (for example the card component defines classes for card body, title, subtitle and so on).</li><li>A plain HTML button looks basic; adding about five Bootstrap classes turns it into a styled button. You only need to know which classes to use, not write the CSS.</li><li>A major reason for its popularity is the 12-column layout system built on Flexbox, designed for responsive, mobile-first sites that look right on phones and desktops.</li><li>Other frameworks: Foundation, MUI, Tailwind and more. Bootstrap holds the largest share among frameworks (roughly 80% of framework users in the figures shown), but the biggest group of sites uses no framework at all.</li><li>Bootstrap does not replace Flexbox, Grid or float knowledge. Learned CSS stays relevant, and you should be able to build without a framework.</li></ul>\n<h3>Pros and cons of CSS frameworks</h3>\n<ul><li>Pros: quick and easy to use; many ready components (pricing plans, cards, navbars); consistent styling across a site; good cross-browser compatibility already tested for you.</li><li>Con: class bloat. Styling lives in the HTML class attributes, which blurs the usual rule of HTML for structure and CSS for style, and markup gets cluttered.</li><li>Con: customisation. If every pixel must follow a custom design, overriding each component is time consuming.</li><li>Good fit: a mobile-first responsive site that must go online fast and look polished and uniform. Poor fit: a very simple page, or a complex bespoke design needing total control.</li></ul>\n<h3>Adding Bootstrap with a CDN</h3>\n<ul><li>A CDN (Content Delivery Network) is a set of servers around the world that serves a file from a location near the visitor, so the Bootstrap CSS downloads quickly.</li><li>Copy the stylesheet link from getbootstrap.com and put it in the head. It is an ordinary link element with rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; whose href points at the CDN file.</li><li>The .min in the filename means minified: whitespace removed so the file is smaller and loads faster. It is unreadable for humans but works the same.</li><li>For interactive features (dropdowns, collapsing menus, and similar), include Bootstrap's script tag just before the closing body tag. This lesson only needs the CSS.</li><li><span class=\"extra\">Extra:</span> The copied link also contains integrity and crossorigin attributes. integrity is a hash the browser checks so a tampered file is rejected.</li></ul>\n<h3>Overriding Bootstrap styles</h3>\n<ul><li>To change a Bootstrap style, your rule must win: use an internal style element, an inline style, or an external stylesheet linked after the Bootstrap link, because later rules override earlier ones of equal specificity.</li><li>Your CSS can build on Bootstrap's rules or define properties Bootstrap never touches.</li><li>In the exercise the card wrapper has a custom class, flex-container, styled by you (not part of Bootstrap).</li></ul>\n<h2>Code examples</h2>\n<p class=\"caption\">Head link for the Bootstrap CSS (version as used in the reference repo)</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;link\n  href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot;\n  rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot;\n  integrity=&quot;sha384-QWTKZyjpPEjISv5WaRU9OFeRpok6YctnYmDr5pNlyT2bRjXh0JMhjY6hW+ALEwIH&quot;\n  crossorigin=&quot;anonymous&quot; /&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Finished exercise body: Bootstrap card inside a centring wrapper</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div class=&quot;flex-container&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot; style=&quot;width: 18rem&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;img src=&quot;./flower.jpg&quot; class=&quot;card-img-top&quot; alt=&quot;Sunflower&quot; /&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;card-body&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;h5 class=&quot;card-title&quot;&gt;Card title&lt;/h5&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;card-text&quot;&gt;Some quick example text for the card.&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;&gt;Go somewhere&lt;/a&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Override style to centre the card</p><pre data-lang=\"css\">.flex-container {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  align-items: center;\n  height: 100vh;\n}</pre>\n<h2>The task: 11.1 Bootstrap Intro: sunflower card</h2>\n<div class=\"task-box\">\n<p><b>Starting point:</b> Starter index.html with four TODO comments, a flower image, goal.png and solution.html.</p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> Use Bootstrap to build a card showing the sunflower image, centred on the page.</p>\n<p><b>Steps</b></p><ol><li>TODO 1: copy the CSS link from getbootstrap.com into the head (CSS only).</li><li>TODO 2: find the Card component in the docs (Components, Card) and paste the first example into the body.</li><li>TODO 3: change the img src from the empty placeholder to the local flower image and add meaningful alt text.</li><li>TODO 4: in an internal style element, give the wrapper (.flex-container) display: flex, justify-content: center, align-items: center and height: 100vh.</li><li>Preview and compare with solution.html.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Expected result:</b> A Bootstrap card (image, title, text and blue button) centred horizontally and vertically.</p>\n</div>\n<p class=\"caption\">Solution</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;link href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot; rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; /&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    .flex-container { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100vh; }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;flex-container&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot; style=&quot;width: 18rem&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;./flower.jpg&quot; class=&quot;card-img-top&quot; alt=&quot;sunflower&quot; /&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;card-body&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;h5 class=&quot;card-title&quot;&gt;Card title&lt;/h5&gt;\n        &lt;p class=&quot;card-text&quot;&gt;Some quick example text.&lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;&gt;Go somewhere&lt;/a&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;</pre>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Leaving the card image src as the docs placeholder, so the image looks broken.</li><li>Linking your own stylesheet before Bootstrap so your overrides lose.</li><li>Forgetting height: 100vh, so vertical centring has no effect.</li><li>Treating the framework as a replacement for CSS knowledge.</li><li><span class=\"extra\">Extra:</span> The reference repo uses a different Bootstrap version between index.html (5.3.3) and solution.html (5.3.0-alpha2), and each page has a personal footer line to ignore.</li></ul>");
PG.notes("l065", "<p class=\"summary\">Explains Bootstrap's container / row / col structure, the 12-column sizing classes, the responsive breakpoints and how to combine several breakpoint classes on one element. Three online exercises (appbrewery.github.io/bootstrap-layout) ask the learner to match a demo's behaviour at each breakpoint by adding col classes; the solution is walked through with trial and error.</p>\n<h3>Container, row, column</h3>\n<ul><li>Three nested pieces: a div.container as the starting point, a div.row inside it, and one or more column divs inside the row.</li><li>A bare class=&quot;col&quot; on several children makes Bootstrap share the row width equally: six cols get a sixth each, three get a third each.</li><li>The container is responsive: its max width changes with the viewport width (roughly 540px on phones, 720 or 960px on tablets, about 1000px+ on desktops, bigger still on wide screens).</li><li>container-{breakpoint} (container-sm, container-md, container-lg, container-xl, container-xxl) is 100% wide below that breakpoint and behaves like a normal container at and above it. Plain container is the same idea as container-sm.</li><li>container-fluid is 100% wide at every size, edge to edge. In practice container and container-fluid are the two used most: container for margins at the sides, fluid for edge-to-edge.</li><li>All these widths refer to the viewport width only.</li></ul>\n<h3>Sized columns (12-column system)</h3>\n<ul><li>Think of each row as 12 equal slots. col-2, col-4, col-6 etc. say how many slots an element occupies, from col-1 to col-12. Bootstrap turns that into a percentage: col-6 is 50%, col-2 is one sixth.</li><li>Example: three divs with col-2, col-4, col-6 fill a full row (2 + 4 + 6 = 12) with no custom CSS.</li><li>Typical use: a navigation column of 2/12 beside main content of 10/12.</li><li>Totals above 12 push the extra column onto the next row. Totals under 12 leave empty space.</li><li>Mixing is allowed: two sized columns (col-2, col-4) plus a plain col means the plain col takes whatever remains.</li></ul>\n<h3>Breakpoints</h3>\n<ul><li>Predefined widths based on common devices: sm (576px and up), md (768px and up), lg (992px and up), xl (1200px and up), xxl (1400px and up). Below 576px is the extra-small range, which has no infix in class names. Rough device mapping: sm phones, md tablets, lg laptops, xl desktops, xxl very large screens.</li><li>Infix classes are min-width based: col-sm-4 applies from the small breakpoint upward. Each class keeps applying at all larger sizes until another class overrides it. Layouts therefore go small first and are tweaked upward.</li><li>Below the smallest breakpoint class used, columns default to full width (stacked), as for col.</li><li>Using col-sm-4 on three elements means three per row from 576px, and stacked on narrower screens.</li><li>Bootstrap's breakpoints reduce the need to write media queries by hand.</li><li>One element can carry several breakpoint classes: for example col-lg-4 col-md-8 col-sm-12 gives 4/12 on large screens, 8/12 on medium and full width on small. Narrower screens usually get larger elements for readability.</li><li><span class=\"extra\">Extra:</span> Bootstrap 5 writes this as col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-4; the unprefixed col-12 covers the smallest range, so col-sm-12 is only needed if you want a distinct step at sm.</li><li>Layout docs: the Layout section of the Bootstrap docs covers breakpoints, containers, columns and the grid system.</li></ul>\n<h3>Solutions to the three online exercises</h3>\n<ul><li>The practice site shows a demo at the top and an editable HTML block below; after editing, press apply changes and resize the window to compare with the demo at each breakpoint.</li><li>Exercise 1: 50% on desktop, 100% on mobile. Add col-xl-6 to both divs (6/12 = 50% at 1200px and up). Below that the default is full width, so adding col-sm-12 is optional.</li><li>Exercise 2 (columns that change at lg and sm): at lg and above, 6/3/3 gives col-lg-6, col-lg-3, col-lg-3. Between sm and lg, first column full width and the other two half each, so the first column has no sm class and the others get col-sm-6. At the smallest size, each column takes 10 of 12 (found by trying 8, seeing it was too narrow, then 10). So a plain col-10 on each.</li><li>Exercise 3 (two columns, five widths): xxl 1 and 11 (col-xxl-1, col-xxl-11); xl 2 and 10; lg 4 and 8; md 6 and 6; below md both full width (an sm class would be redundant).</li><li>Each pair of numbers adds up to 12 so both columns stay on one row.</li><li>Method: start at the largest breakpoint, estimate proportions by eye (or with a ruler), apply, then step down. Trial and error is fine.</li><li>Finding breakpoint widths: in Chrome DevTools toggle the device toolbar, choose Responsive and drag the width bar while watching the pixel number, e.g. a jump at 1200px indicates xl.</li></ul>\n<h2>Code examples</h2>\n<p class=\"caption\">Container, row and sized columns (2 + 4 + 6 = 12)</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;col-2&quot;&gt;2 of 12&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;col-4&quot;&gt;4 of 12&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;col-6&quot;&gt;6 of 12&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Equal columns with a bare col, and mixing sized with remainder</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col&quot;&gt;equal&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col&quot;&gt;equal&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col&quot;&gt;equal&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-2&quot;&gt;fixed 2&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-4&quot;&gt;fixed 4&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col&quot;&gt;takes the remaining 6&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Several breakpoint classes on one element</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-4 col-md-8 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;4/12 on lg+, 8/12 on md, full width on sm&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Exercise solutions (reconstructed from the walkthrough)</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!-- Exercise 1: 50% on desktop, 100% below --&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-xl-6&quot;&gt;A&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-xl-6&quot;&gt;B&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;!-- Exercise 2 --&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-10 col-lg-6&quot;&gt;1&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-10 col-sm-6 col-lg-3&quot;&gt;2&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-10 col-sm-6 col-lg-3&quot;&gt;3&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;!-- Exercise 3 --&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-md-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-2 col-xxl-1&quot;&gt;1&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-md-6 col-lg-8 col-xl-10 col-xxl-11&quot;&gt;2&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<h2>The task: Bootstrap layout practice site (appbrewery.github.io/bootstrap-layout)</h2>\n<div class=\"task-box\">\n<p><b>Starting point:</b> Online page with three exercises, each showing a demo area on top and an editable HTML snippet for your area underneath.</p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> Add Bootstrap grid classes so your area reacts to window width exactly like the demo at every breakpoint.</p>\n<p><b>Steps</b></p><ol><li>Open the practice site and read the description of exercise 1: 50% width on desktop, 100% on mobile.</li><li>Edit the HTML using col-{breakpoint}-{n} classes; press apply changes.</li><li>Resize the window and compare with the demo at each breakpoint; use DevTools responsive mode to see the pixel width.</li><li>Repeat for exercise 2 (columns that change at lg and sm, and a narrow-screen width) and exercise 3 (two columns, proportions changing at xxl, xl, lg, md).</li><li>Check the Layout section of the Bootstrap docs if stuck.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Expected result:</b> Your area is indistinguishable from the demo as the window shrinks through each breakpoint.</p>\n</div>\n<p class=\"caption\">Solution</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!-- Ex1 --&gt;  col-xl-6 on both\n&lt;!-- Ex2 --&gt;  [col-10 col-lg-6] [col-10 col-sm-6 col-lg-3] [col-10 col-sm-6 col-lg-3]\n&lt;!-- Ex3 --&gt;  [col-md-6 col-lg-4 col-xl-2 col-xxl-1] [col-md-6 col-lg-8 col-xl-10 col-xxl-11]</pre>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting that breakpoint classes mean that size and above, not just that size.</li><li>Column numbers that do not add to 12 wrapping to a new row unexpectedly.</li><li>Missing the row wrapper: cols must sit in a row, which sits in a container.</li><li>Giving up on trial and error; matching a target by eye and adjusting is a normal workflow.</li><li><span class=\"extra\">Extra:</span> The exercise solutions above for 2 and 3 are reconstructed from the spoken walkthrough, so verify against the practice site. No reference repo folder exists for this lecture.</li></ul>");
PG.notes("s11-components", "<p class=\"summary\">Shows how Bootstrap components (buttons, cards, navbar, carousel, footer) are used by copying documentation or Examples snippets and editing text, images and classes. Builds the one-page 'Move It' moving-company site section by section, then covers spacing utilities, dark mode via data-bs-theme and where to find themes.</p>\n<h3>Components are class names on ordinary HTML</h3>\n<ul><li>A component is a pre-styled UI piece (button, card, carousel, navbar) obtained just by adding Bootstrap classes to normal elements. No CSS has to be written for the basic look.</li><li>Workflow: open getbootstrap.com, Docs, Components, find the component, copy the example markup, paste it into the page, then swap the text, image src and alt text.</li><li>The Examples and Snippets areas (Headers, Heroes, Features, Footers) offer larger multi-component layouts that can be lifted the same way.</li></ul>\n<h3>Buttons and the colour names</h3>\n<ul><li>A button needs the base class btn plus a colour class: btn-primary (default blue, used for main actions), btn-success, btn-danger, btn-warning and so on. The names hint at meaning (success for OK, danger for risky actions).</li><li>btn alone changes the font, padding, border and rounded corners; the colour class adds the background and hover behaviour.</li><li>Exercise result: &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-success&quot;&gt;Ok&lt;/button&gt; gives a green button with hover animation.</li></ul>\n<h3>Navbar</h3>\n<ul><li>Copy a navbar example from Components &gt; Navbar (the version with brand, links, a dropdown and a search form is the starting point here). Paste it just inside body.</li><li>Below the lg breakpoint the links collapse behind a hamburger button (navbar-toggler). That button and the dropdown only work if Bootstrap's JavaScript bundle is loaded.</li><li>Fix: add the bootstrap.bundle.min.js script tag from the CDN (the second CDN link from the setup lesson) just before the closing body tag. data-bs-toggle and data-bs-target attributes on the toggler, dropdown and carousel are what the script hooks into.</li><li>Customising: delete the 'disabled' list item (a nav-link with the disabled class cannot be clicked), rename links (Link to About, Dropdown to Services), keep or trim dropdown-menu items.</li><li>navbar-brand holds the site name; an img inside it works as a logo. Control size with a height attribute (30 here) because raw images are far too large.</li><li>The form on the right is only restyled: change the input placeholder to Postcode and the button text to Check. Forms get real behaviour later in the back-end sections.</li><li>Inspecting a nav-link in dev tools shows how much CSS (padding, toggle styles, states) Bootstrap supplies for a single navbar item.</li></ul>\n<h3>Bootstrap Icons and SVGs</h3>\n<ul><li>Bootstrap Icons (the Icons page) are free to use in any project. Search with the filter, e.g. box-seam for the moving-box logo.</li><li>Two ways to use an icon: paste the inline &lt;svg&gt; markup, or download the .svg file into the project and reference it with an img tag (src, alt, height). The lecture chooses the img route for a cleaner page.</li><li>Icons used: box-seam (brand), briefcase, bus-front, chat-square-heart (feature icons), chevron-right (link arrow).</li></ul>\n<h3>Hero section copied from Examples</h3>\n<ul><li>Examples &gt; Heroes has a centred hero: heading, paragraph, two buttons and an image. Technique: right-click, Inspect, hover up the element tree until the whole section is highlighted, Copy element, then paste below the navbar.</li><li>Replace the image src with the moving van, paste the h1 'Move With Joy', the paragraph and button labels (Get a Quote, Contact Us) from the provided website-text file.</li><li>Useful classes in it: display-4 fw-bold (big bold heading), lead (larger intro paragraph), col-lg-6 mx-auto (centred half-width column), d-grid gap-2 d-sm-flex justify-content-sm-center (buttons stacked on phones, inline from sm), img-fluid rounded-3 shadow-lg border.</li></ul>\n<h3>Features section and custom CSS</h3>\n<ul><li>Same copy-element technique from Examples &gt; Features (three columns with icon squares). Replace the headings and text with Professional, Countrywide and Personal Touch.</li><li>Pasted result looks unstyled in the icon squares because Examples pages add their own CSS on top of Bootstrap. Class names like feature-icon do not exist in Bootstrap itself.</li><li>How to spot custom CSS: default classes live in Bootstrap's stylesheet, while page-specific ones appear in a separate custom file. Copy the .feature-icon rules (width and height 4rem, border-radius 0.75rem) into the page's style block.</li><li>Swap the example SVGs for your downloaded icon images and give each a height of 30. Do the same for the chevron-right in each 'Get a quote' icon-link.</li><li>The layout classes row, row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-3 and g-4 produce one column on mobile and three on large screens.</li></ul>\n<h3>Carousel (exercise) and container</h3>\n<ul><li>Carousel = slideshow component. Use the basic 'With indicators' example from Components &gt; Carousel; it gives dots at the bottom plus previous and next arrows.</li><li>Pasted images are broken because the example img tags have no usable src. Set them to couple, dog and family images.</li><li>Structure: .carousel &gt; .carousel-indicators (buttons with data-bs-slide-to index), .carousel-inner &gt; .carousel-item (exactly one has active), and prev/next controls using data-bs-slide. The id on the carousel must match every data-bs-target.</li><li>Because the carousel spans the viewport width it is huge. Wrap it in a div.container to line it up with other content and get responsive widths.</li></ul>\n<h3>Footer</h3>\n<ul><li>Taken from Snippets &gt; Footers: inspect, copy the footer element and place it last in the body. Only light editing is needed.</li></ul>\n<h3>Spacing utilities</h3>\n<ul><li>Pattern: property + side + dash + size. Property m = margin, p = padding.</li><li>Sides: t top, b bottom, s start (left), e end (right), x left and right, y top and bottom, none = all sides. Sizes 0 to 5 (0 removes spacing, 5 is the largest standard step).</li><li>Examples: mt-5 margin-top size 5; my-3 vertical margin size 3; mb-2 margin-bottom size 2 (seen in the footer markup).</li><li><span class=\"extra\">Extra:</span> Beware that the lecture describes x and y with the axes swapped in speech; in Bootstrap x is horizontal (left and right) and y is vertical (top and bottom).</li></ul>\n<h3>Dark mode</h3>\n<ul><li>Add data-bs-theme=&quot;dark&quot; on the html element (after lang) and the whole page switches to the dark colour scheme.</li><li>Docs location: Customize &gt; Color modes. With JavaScript later, the attribute can be toggled to let users choose.</li><li><span class=\"extra\">Extra:</span> The attribute can also be set on a single element to theme only that region.</li></ul>\n<h3>Themes and templates</h3>\n<ul><li>Hosted builders charge a monthly fee; Bootstrap themes are typically a one-off purchase or free.</li><li>Sources mentioned: W3Schools Bootstrap templates (basic blog, portfolio, social layouts to customise), the official Themes page on getbootstrap.com (professional, paid), and web searches for free Bootstrap templates.</li><li>Approach is the same as in the lesson: pick a template, grab the parts needed, customise with some own CSS. Designers can also build and sell themes.</li></ul>\n<h2>Code examples</h2>\n<p class=\"caption\">Green button (exercise)</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-success&quot;&gt;Ok&lt;/button&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Move It navbar (trimmed from reference solution)</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;nav class=&quot;navbar navbar-expand-lg bg-body-tertiary&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;container-fluid&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;a class=&quot;navbar-brand&quot; href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./box-seam.svg&quot; alt=&quot;moveit brand icon&quot; height=&quot;30&quot; /&gt; Move It&lt;/a&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;navbar-toggler&quot; type=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-toggle=&quot;collapse&quot;\n      data-bs-target=&quot;#navbarSupportedContent&quot; aria-controls=&quot;navbarSupportedContent&quot;\n      aria-expanded=&quot;false&quot; aria-label=&quot;Toggle navigation&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;span class=&quot;navbar-toggler-icon&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;collapse navbar-collapse&quot; id=&quot;navbarSupportedContent&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;ul class=&quot;navbar-nav me-auto mb-2 mb-lg-0&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;li class=&quot;nav-item&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;nav-link active&quot; aria-current=&quot;page&quot; href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li class=&quot;nav-item&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;nav-link&quot; href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li class=&quot;nav-item dropdown&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;a class=&quot;nav-link dropdown-toggle&quot; href=&quot;#&quot; role=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-toggle=&quot;dropdown&quot; aria-expanded=&quot;false&quot;&gt;Services&lt;/a&gt;\n          &lt;ul class=&quot;dropdown-menu&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;dropdown-item&quot; href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Action&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n            &lt;li&gt;&lt;hr class=&quot;dropdown-divider&quot; /&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n            &lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;dropdown-item&quot; href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Something else here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n          &lt;/ul&gt;\n        &lt;/li&gt;\n      &lt;/ul&gt;\n      &lt;form class=&quot;d-flex&quot; role=&quot;search&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;input class=&quot;form-control me-2&quot; type=&quot;search&quot; placeholder=&quot;Postcode&quot; aria-label=&quot;Search&quot; /&gt;\n        &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-outline-success&quot; type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Check&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;/form&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/nav&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Hero section</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div class=&quot;px-4 pt-5 my-5 text-center border-bottom&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;h1 class=&quot;display-4 fw-bold text-body-emphasis&quot;&gt;Move With Joy&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-6 mx-auto&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;lead mb-4&quot;&gt;...paragraph from website-text...&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;d-grid gap-2 d-sm-flex justify-content-sm-center mb-5&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary btn-lg px-4 me-sm-3&quot;&gt;Get a Quote&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg px-4&quot;&gt;Contact Us&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;overflow-hidden&quot; style=&quot;max-height: 30vh&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;container px-5&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;img src=&quot;./moving-van.jpg&quot; class=&quot;img-fluid border rounded-3 shadow-lg mb-4&quot; alt=&quot;Example image&quot; width=&quot;700&quot; height=&quot;500&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; /&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Features section with custom CSS</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;style&gt;\n  .feature-icon { width: 4rem; height: 4rem; border-radius: 0.75rem; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n...\n&lt;div class=&quot;container px-4 py-5&quot; id=&quot;featured-3&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;h2 class=&quot;pb-2 border-bottom&quot;&gt;Why Move With Us?&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;row g-4 py-5 row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-3&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;feature col&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;feature-icon d-inline-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-bg-primary bg-gradient fs-2 mb-3&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;img src=&quot;./briefcase.svg&quot; alt=&quot;briefcase&quot; height=&quot;30&quot; /&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;h3 class=&quot;fs-2&quot;&gt;Professional&lt;/h3&gt;\n      &lt;p&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; class=&quot;icon-link&quot;&gt;Get a quote &lt;img src=&quot;./chevron-right.svg&quot; alt=&quot;chevron-right&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;!-- two more .feature.col blocks: bus-front.svg (Countrywide), chat-square-heart.svg (Personal Touch) --&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Carousel inside a container</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div id=&quot;carouselExampleIndicators&quot; class=&quot;carousel slide&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;carousel-indicators&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-target=&quot;#carouselExampleIndicators&quot; data-bs-slide-to=&quot;0&quot; class=&quot;active&quot; aria-current=&quot;true&quot; aria-label=&quot;Slide 1&quot;&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-target=&quot;#carouselExampleIndicators&quot; data-bs-slide-to=&quot;1&quot; aria-label=&quot;Slide 2&quot;&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-target=&quot;#carouselExampleIndicators&quot; data-bs-slide-to=&quot;2&quot; aria-label=&quot;Slide 3&quot;&gt;&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;carousel-inner&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;carousel-item active&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./couple.jpg&quot; class=&quot;d-block w-100&quot; alt=&quot;couple&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;carousel-item&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./dog.jpg&quot; class=&quot;d-block w-100&quot; alt=&quot;dog&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;carousel-item&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./family.jpg&quot; class=&quot;d-block w-100&quot; alt=&quot;family&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;carousel-control-prev&quot; type=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-target=&quot;#carouselExampleIndicators&quot; data-bs-slide=&quot;prev&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;span class=&quot;carousel-control-prev-icon&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;span class=&quot;visually-hidden&quot;&gt;Previous&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;carousel-control-next&quot; type=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-target=&quot;#carouselExampleIndicators&quot; data-bs-slide=&quot;next&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;span class=&quot;carousel-control-next-icon&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;span class=&quot;visually-hidden&quot;&gt;Next&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Dark mode and the JS bundle</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot; data-bs-theme=&quot;dark&quot;&gt;\n...\n  &lt;script src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0-alpha3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;</pre>\n<h2>The task: 11.2 Bootstrap Components: Move It website</h2>\n<div class=\"task-box\">\n<p><b>Starting point:</b> Starter folder with index.html (Bootstrap CSS link already added, empty style block), website-text file, SVG icons (box-seam, briefcase, bus-front, chat-square-heart, chevron-right) and images (moving-van, couple, dog, family).</p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> Two small challenges inside a guided build: (1) add a green Ok button using the Buttons docs; (2) add a carousel section with three images, aligned with the page content. The guided build is a one-page Move It site: navbar, hero, features, carousel, footer.</p>\n<p><b>Steps</b></p><ol><li>Download and open the 11.2 starter files in VS Code and preview them.</li><li>Challenge 1: find Buttons in the docs and add a button saying Ok with btn and btn-success.</li><li>Paste the navbar example into body, then add the Bootstrap JS bundle script before &lt;/body&gt; so the toggler and dropdown work.</li><li>Edit the navbar: remove the disabled item, rename links to About and Services, set brand to Move It with the box-seam image (height 30), set placeholder Postcode and button text Check.</li><li>Copy the hero element from Examples, set the image to the moving van, paste texts from website-text.</li><li>Copy the Features example, fill in texts, add the .feature-icon CSS to the style block, replace the SVGs with the downloaded icons with height 30.</li><li>Challenge 2: from Components &gt; Carousel copy the indicators example, set the three img src values (couple, dog, family) and wrap the carousel in div.container.</li><li>Add a footer from Snippets &gt; Footers. Optionally try data-bs-theme=&quot;dark&quot; on html.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Expected result:</b> A responsive one-page site with collapsing navbar, centred hero, three feature columns with icons, a working three-slide carousel inside a container, and a footer.</p>\n</div>\n<p class=\"caption\">Solution</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!-- See code_examples: navbar, hero, features, carousel; footer copied from Snippets &gt; Footers --&gt;\n&lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-success&quot;&gt;Ok&lt;/button&gt;</pre>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Navbar toggler and dropdowns do nothing unless the bootstrap.bundle.min.js script is included.</li><li>Copied Examples may rely on page-specific CSS (feature-icon) that has to be copied too.</li><li>Broken carousel images: the example has no real src values.</li><li>Carousel without a container fills the full width and becomes very tall.</li><li>Carousel indicator and control data-bs-target values must match the carousel's id.</li><li>Reference repo diverges: uses Bootstrap 5.3.0-alpha CDN, keeps leftover placeholder text such as Action items, a stray svg use tag in the footer and a personal author footer line (ignore it).</li></ul>");
PG.notes("s11-tindog", "<p class=\"summary\">Project brief and full walkthrough for building the TinDog landing page (hero, features, testimonial, pricing, footer) purely from Bootstrap Examples/Snippets plus a little custom CSS. The walkthrough shows how to copy a snippet, fix what breaks, and tune it with utility classes.</p>\n<h3>Project setup and provided assets</h3>\n<ul><li>The starter has index.html with a comment-labelled section element per area (title, features, testimonial, pricing, contact/footer), an images folder (iphone.png, dog-img.jpg, four press logos), goal screenshots per section, and a README with the copy text and ready-made SVG icons.</li><li>section elements group distinct areas of a page and keep the code organised; each part of the build goes inside its section.</li><li>Use the README SVGs rather than the ones in Bootstrap's snippets because sizes differ. Copy all text from the README or the live demo (in real work the client usually supplies the copy).</li><li>The provided style.css already contains .gradient-background: a three-colour linear-gradient with background-size 180% and a long looping @keyframes animation that slides background-position. Applying that single class animates any element.</li><li>Reference finished site: appbrewery.github.io/tindog. Expect 30-60 minutes of independent attempt before watching.</li></ul>\n<h3>Link order: Bootstrap first, custom CSS second</h3>\n<ul><li>If a pasted snippet looks like raw HTML (wrong font, unstyled buttons), the Bootstrap CSS link is missing. Take the link from the docs home page and add it to head.</li><li>Add the custom stylesheet link after Bootstrap's so that equal-specificity rules from your file win.</li></ul>\n<h3>Hero (Title section)</h3>\n<ul><li>Use Examples &gt; Heroes (text left, image right). Inspect, climb to the top-level element after the divider, copy the element, paste into the title section.</li><li>Fix the image: src to images/iphone.png, alt 'app demo'. Remove the width attribute and set height 200 so the aspect ratio is kept.</li><li>Replace the h1 with the headline, delete the paragraph, change both buttons to read Download and paste the Apple and Google Play SVGs before the text (with a space).</li><li>Colours: btn-primary becomes btn-light, btn-outline-secondary becomes btn-outline-light. A white outline button is nearly invisible on white, which is why the gradient is needed.</li><li>Put gradient-background on the section element, not the inner container, otherwise the gradient stops at the container's side margins. It is a class, so use the class attribute, not id.</li><li>Excess spacing: padding extends the background colour, margin does not (margin would show white). Hover in dev tools to see the orange padding box, find the py-5 classes on the container and the row div and change them to pt-5 so only top padding remains.</li></ul>\n<h3>Features section</h3>\n<ul><li>Source: Snippets &gt; Features (three columns, icon, heading, text). Copy the row element.</li><li>A bare .row spans full width and misaligns with the rest of the page; wrapping it in a .container (moving the closing tag to wrap everything) lines it up.</li><li>Remove the snippet's extra link/button anchors, replace text, then swap the icons for the README SVGs (check mark, graduation hat, heart with arrow).</li><li>Icon backgrounds look wrong because the snippet's .icon-square (a div with fancy styling) is custom CSS from the example page, not Bootstrap. Find it via Inspect &gt; Styles, copy the rule into style.css.</li><li>Add mt-5 on the container for spacing from the hero (the goal image hints at this).</li></ul>\n<h3>Testimonial and press logos</h3>\n<ul><li>Source: Examples &gt; Jumbotrons (full-width jumbotron). Copy the section after the divider and paste into testimonial.</li><li>Change the h1 to an h2 for the quote since the page should only have one h1 (already used in the hero). Keep the paragraph for the attribution 'Pebbles, New York'.</li><li>Add the dog image between them, with a custom class .profile-img: height 100px and border-radius 50% for a circle. Spacing: mt-5 on the image, mt-2 on the paragraph.</li><li>Press logos: new .container &gt; .row, each logo in a column with col-lg-3 col-sm-12 (four across on desktop, stacked on small screens). Each img gets alt text and height 30 so they line up.</li><li><span class=\"extra\">Extra:</span> col-sm-12 only affects widths of 576px and up; below that, columns without a col-* class already stack, so it is redundant but harmless.</li></ul>\n<h3>Pricing</h3>\n<ul><li>Source: Snippets &gt; Pricing. Copy the row with three cards and wrap it in a container (a row must live in a container). Also copy the heading block above the cards and put it at the top of the container.</li><li>Colour changes: primary becomes dark across the buttons and highlighted card header/border (btn-outline-dark, btn-dark, text-bg-dark, border-dark).</li><li>Use the editor's find with replace one match at a time rather than Replace All, so only the intended spots change.</li><li>The snippet's heading is an h1; change it to h2 (title) and the subtitle to a paragraph. Appearance is unchanged because display-4 and fs-5 classes control size, not the tag. Bootstrap classes are independent of semantics, so fix semantics separately.</li><li>Card structure: .card &gt; .card-header + .card-body &gt; card-title, list-unstyled ul, full-width button (w-100 btn btn-lg).</li></ul>\n<h3>Footer</h3>\n<ul><li>Source: Snippets &gt; Footers. Copy the container holding the footer into the footer section.</li><li>Remove the Bootstrap-logo link at the top left, change the copyright paragraph to the company name, leave the placeholder links.</li><li>Remove border-top from the footer element to drop the line. Add gradient-background to the footer's section.</li><li>The white strip underneath is the bottom margin from my-5; changing it to mt-5 removes it, keeping top spacing.</li></ul>\n<h3>Take-aways</h3>\n<ul><li>Workflow repeated for each section: find the closest snippet, copy the element, wrap in container if needed, fix images/text/icons, compare with goal image, inspect to track down missing styles, adjust with utilities.</li><li>Bootstrap suits quickly assembling modern-looking pages from components; Flexbox and Grid suit fully custom layouts.</li></ul>\n<h2>Code examples</h2>\n<p class=\"caption\">Head links and hero section</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;link href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0-alpha3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot; rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;./css/style.css&quot; /&gt;   &lt;!-- custom CSS AFTER Bootstrap so it wins --&gt;\n...\n&lt;section id=&quot;title&quot; class=&quot;gradient-background&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;container col-xxl-8 px-4 pt-5&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;row flex-lg-row-reverse align-items-center g-5 pt-5&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col-10 col-sm-8 col-lg-6&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;img src=&quot;./images/iphone.png&quot; class=&quot;d-block mx-lg-auto img-fluid&quot; alt=&quot;app demo&quot; height=&quot;200&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; /&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-6&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;h1 class=&quot;display-5 fw-bold text-body-emphasis lh-1 mb-3&quot;&gt;Meet new and interesting dogs nearby.&lt;/h1&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;d-grid gap-2 d-md-flex justify-content-md-start&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-light btn-lg px-4 me-md-2&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;svg class=&quot;bi bi-apple mb-1&quot; ...&gt;&lt;!-- Apple icon pasted from the README --&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; Download\n          &lt;/button&gt;\n          &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-light btn-lg px-4&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;svg class=&quot;bi bi-google-play mb-1&quot; ...&gt;&lt;!-- Google Play icon from README --&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; Download\n          &lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/section&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Features section (one of three items)</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;section id=&quot;features&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;container mt-5&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;row g-4 py-5 row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-3&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col d-flex align-items-start&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;icon-square text-body-emphasis bg-body-secondary d-inline-flex align-items-center justify-content-center fs-4 flex-shrink-0 me-3&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;svg class=&quot;bi bi-check2-circle&quot; height=&quot;30&quot; fill=&quot;currentColor&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 16 16&quot;&gt;...&lt;/svg&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div&gt;\n          &lt;h3 class=&quot;fs-2&quot;&gt;Easy to use.&lt;/h3&gt;\n          &lt;p&gt;So easy to use, even your dog could do it.&lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;!-- Elite Clientele (bi-mortarboard) and Guaranteed to work (bi-arrow-through-heart) repeat the same shape --&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/section&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Testimonial and press logos</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;section id=&quot;testimonial&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;my-5&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;p-5 text-center bg-body-tertiary&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;container py-5&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;h2 class=&quot;text-body-emphasis&quot;&gt;&quot;I no longer have to sniff other dogs for love. I've found the hottest Corgi on TinDog. Woof.&quot;&lt;/h2&gt;\n        &lt;img class=&quot;profile-img mt-5&quot; src=&quot;./images/dog-img.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;dog image&quot; /&gt;\n        &lt;p class=&quot;col-lg-8 mx-auto lead mt-2&quot;&gt;Pebbles, New York&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-3 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./images/techcrunch.png&quot; alt=&quot;techcrunch&quot; height=&quot;30&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-3 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./images/mashable.png&quot; alt=&quot;mashable&quot; height=&quot;30&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-3 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./images/bizinsider.png&quot; alt=&quot;bizinsider&quot; height=&quot;30&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-3 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;./images/tnw.png&quot; alt=&quot;tnw&quot; height=&quot;30&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/section&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Pricing section (first card, others described)</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;section id=&quot;pricing&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;pricing-header p-3 pb-md-4 mx-auto text-center&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;h2 class=&quot;display-4 fw-normal&quot;&gt;A Plan for Every Dog's Needs&lt;/h2&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;fs-5 text-body-secondary&quot;&gt;Simple and affordable price plans for you and your dog.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-3 mb-3 text-center&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;card mb-4 rounded-3 shadow-sm&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;card-header py-3&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 class=&quot;my-0 fw-normal&quot;&gt;Chihuahua&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;card-body&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;h1 class=&quot;card-title pricing-card-title&quot;&gt;$0&lt;small class=&quot;text-body-secondary fw-light&quot;&gt;/mo&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;\n            &lt;ul class=&quot;list-unstyled mt-3 mb-4&quot;&gt;\n              &lt;li&gt;5 Matches Per Day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;10 Messages Per Day&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Unlimited App Usage&lt;/li&gt;\n            &lt;/ul&gt;\n            &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;w-100 btn btn-lg btn-outline-dark&quot;&gt;Sign up for free&lt;/button&gt;\n          &lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;!-- Labrador $15: plain card, button btn-dark &quot;Get started&quot; --&gt;\n      &lt;!-- Mastiff $29: card gets border-dark, header gets text-bg-dark border-dark, button btn-dark &quot;Contact us&quot; --&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/section&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">Footer section</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;section id=&quot;contact&quot; class=&quot;gradient-background&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;footer class=&quot;row row-cols-1 row-cols-sm-2 row-cols-md-5 py-5 mt-5&quot;&gt;   &lt;!-- border-top removed, my-5 became mt-5 --&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col mb-3&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;text-body-secondary&quot;&gt;&amp;copy; TinDog&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col mb-3&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col mb-3&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;h5&gt;Section&lt;/h5&gt;\n        &lt;ul class=&quot;nav flex-column&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;li class=&quot;nav-item mb-2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; class=&quot;nav-link p-0 text-body-secondary&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n          &lt;!-- Features, Pricing, FAQs, About ... and two more identical columns --&gt;\n        &lt;/ul&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/footer&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/section&gt;</pre>\n<p class=\"caption\">css/style.css: gradient, icon-square, profile-img</p><pre data-lang=\"css\">.gradient-background {\n  background: linear-gradient(300deg, #00bfff, #ff4c68, #ef8172);\n  background-size: 180% 180%;\n  animation: gradient-animation 18s ease infinite;\n}\n@keyframes gradient-animation {\n  0%   { background-position: 0% 50%; }\n  50%  { background-position: 100% 50%; }\n  100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }\n}\n.icon-square { width: 3rem; height: 3rem; border-radius: 0.75rem; }\n.profile-img { border-radius: 50%; height: 100px; }</pre>\n<h2>The task: 11.3 TinDog Project</h2>\n<div class=\"task-box\">\n<p><b>Starting point:</b> Starter folder: index.html with empty section elements and comments, css/style.css containing .gradient-background, images folder, goal images for title, features, testimonial, pricing and footer, README with copy text and SVG code. No Bootstrap link yet.</p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> Reproduce the TinDog landing page (gradient hero with download buttons and phone image, three features, testimonial with logos, three-plan pricing, gradient footer) that is responsive on desktop and phone.</p>\n<p><b>Steps</b></p><ol><li>Link Bootstrap CSS (and then the custom style.css after it) in head.</li><li>Hero: copy the Heroes example, set iphone.png with height 200, add heading, remove paragraph, two Download buttons with README SVGs using btn-light and btn-outline-light, add gradient-background to the section and trim padding with pt-5.</li><li>Features: copy the Features snippet, wrap in container mt-5, remove link buttons, insert text and SVGs, copy the icon-square CSS.</li><li>Testimonial: copy the Jumbotron, h1 to h2, add circular profile image (.profile-img), build the four press logos with a container, row and col-lg-3 col-sm-12 columns, height 30.</li><li>Pricing: copy the three-card row inside a container, add the heading block, insert plan text (Chihuahua, Labrador, Mastiff), switch primary to dark one by one, make title h2 and subtitle p.</li><li>Footer: copy a footer snippet, remove logo link, set copyright to TinDog, remove border-top, give the section gradient-background and change my-5 to mt-5.</li><li>Compare each section with its goal image and test at phone width.</li></ol>\n<p><b>Expected result:</b> A page matching appbrewery.github.io/tindog: animated blue/red/peach gradient hero and footer, responsive layout.</p>\n</div>\n<p class=\"caption\">Solution</p><pre data-lang=\"html\">&lt;!-- Full structure shown in code_examples. Reference: css/solution.css + solution.html. --&gt;\n&lt;section id=&quot;title&quot; class=&quot;gradient-background&quot;&gt;...&lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;section id=&quot;features&quot;&gt;...&lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;section id=&quot;testimonial&quot;&gt;...&lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;section id=&quot;pricing&quot;&gt;...&lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;section id=&quot;contact&quot; class=&quot;gradient-background&quot;&gt;...&lt;/section&gt;</pre>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting the Bootstrap link so the pasted snippet appears unstyled.</li><li>Placing the custom CSS link before Bootstrap, letting Bootstrap override it.</li><li>Putting gradient-background on the inner container instead of the full-width section.</li><li>Mixing up padding (extends the background) and margin (shows page white).</li><li>A row outside a container makes content run edge to edge.</li><li>Replace All on 'primary' can change unrelated places; step through the matches.</li><li>Using more than one h1 on the page.</li><li>Reference repo diverges: uses Bootstrap 5.3.0-alpha3, keeps the author footer line (ignore), has a typo in a pricing item (priority), and an alt text left as 'Bootstrap Themes' in the hero image.</li></ul>");
